ison, which is a load-bearing correctness detail in the very precedent it cites. In scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py the shrink-only lock had to be changed to compare against merge-base(main, HEAD) rather than main's tip (bug humble-cinnamoned-mussel): against the tip, once any landed change LOWERS a baseline entry, every un-rebased branch still carrying the old file reads as RAISING it, so the ratchet starts failing the shrinking it exists to reward. An AC5 child implemented against main's tip would inherit that already-fixed defect.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1c1607a09c6c7933","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria — AC5 (mechanism ratchet)","norm_id":"n5d7449338e034c5e","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A mechanism is removed/justified on main, lowering the baseline; an older open branch runs make lint and the ratchet spuriously fails it as an unjustified addition","Shallow CI checkout with no shared history reaches the ratchet"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Amend AC5 to require the ratchet compare against merge-base(main, HEAD), following the shrink-only-baseline precedent's comparison basis and its fail-closed fallback to main's tip when no merge base exists.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","intern